This setter is a single forwarding call, so there is little real speedup available. The rewrite keeps exactly the same call and arguments. The only changes are hoisting the subfield index into a `constexpr` constant and replacing the C-style cast with `static_cast`. This guarantees the index is a compile-time constant and leaves behavior unchanged.

```cpp
    void SetTotalStrokes(FIT_UINT32 totalStrokes)
    {
        constexpr FIT_UINT16 kSubField = static_cast<FIT_UINT16>(Profile::SEGMENT_LAP_MESG_TOTAL_CYCLES_FIELD_TOTAL_STROKES);
        SetFieldUINT32Value(10, totalStrokes, 0, kSubField);
    }
```